From b267fbab49c30721cbd6ad8f91f8a4b4ad410cab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:57:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Show a stereoscopic 3D video in 3D, with a 3D menu

The 3D video's stream says how it is packed and Qt Multimedia's VideoOutput
shows it as it should be: both views to the compositor where it takes stereo
content, one view elsewhere. Plank Player only needs a menu to choose what is
shown, and how the views are packed in a video that does not say, or says it
wrong, and to read the shape of an unmarked wide video as side by side.

The menu is reached with the remote control's keys, from the 3D button of the
on-screen display.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
